{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793451251,"nonce":"5TNFrfyIyt99bNW2JhOZYGygJ9I=","message":"Decision (darmie): open question 1 is settled. The AEL runtime is not embedded in nan8 and needs no host process of nan8's: it runs as an actor on dynASB, which invokes the Zyntax JIT, and AEL's effects cross as actor messages (effect request as an emit with the EffectId as idempotency key; completion and pending-handle notification as inbound messages). Zyntax also gives dynASB sandboxed Python, Lua and TypeScript scripting. Tracked in dynASB 5b7d11d. nan8 then holds the effect handlers' counterparts (sandbox API, model and memory routing, metering), not the runtime.","files":null}]}